    // it; emitFunc hands the answer on through genClosure, so the closure that body
    // belongs to knows to wrap itself. csHasIter is the walk-time twin: it says whether the
    // PROGRAM has any iterator at all, and gates the generator branch of foreach - a
    // program without one emits the plain index loop it emitted before. GetEnumerator /
    // MoveNext / Current need no such gate: they are only reached from a site that names
    // them, and they work on an array whether or not the program declares an iterator.
